{"requirements":[{"id":"gateway","requirement":"Node1 accepts OTLP/HTTP over HTTPS on port 4318 and requires the supplied client certificate.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After all restarts, node1 was healthy and listening on 4318; authenticated OTLP/HTTP requests succeeded while a request without a client certificate failed during TLS negotiation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-70b5b11a8bd04bb3","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"routing","requirement":"Route payments only to node2 and inventory only to node3, while rejecting missing or unsupported service.namespace values.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final tests returned 200 for payments and inventory and 503 for missing and unsupported namespaces. Backend inspection found the expected namespace only, with no cross-routed or rejected proofs.","evidence_ids":["cmd-70b5b11a8bd04bb3","cmd-7aa1fe6755c84340","cmd-97f32e629e844972"]},{"id":"collector_mtls","requirement":"Use mutual TLS between node1 and the backend collectors.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 authenticated successfully to both backend certificates with CA verification, and both node2 and node3 rejected TLS connections lacking a client certificate.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4fec6a9e3edc4003","cmd-9887ff6ee12f4f30"]},{"id":"retention_delivery","requirement":"Retain payments in /var/lib/otel/payments.json and inventory in /var/lib/otel/inventory.json without cross-routing or duplicate delivery.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final files existed at the required paths and contained each selected pre-restart, post-restart, and final proof once, with zero opposite-namespace or rejected proofs. Corrected append-mode restart tests directly demonstrated persistence and subsequent appending.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8a79ae18f18140b0","cmd-6d3e047f53f745fc","cmd-893b53be68424aa4","cmd-c29240b62c1e4e2b","cmd-efdd6750ecca4f01","cmd-25abea78377f4c3d","cmd-7aa1fe6755c84340","cmd-97f32e629e844972"]},{"id":"client_credentials","requirement":"Provide client credentials under /root/otel-client on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The CA certificate, client certificate, and client private key were present after restart; the private key had mode 0600 and was successfully used for final requests.","evidence_ids":["cmd-23be569905bc42d6","cmd-70b5b11a8bd04bb3"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.76,"summary":"Final system hygiene was generally sound: no failed services or damaged package state remained. Avoidable transient mutations included initially enabling backend services with unreadable certificate paths, producing restart loops before correction (cmd-2dadcd08ff95497a, cmd-4f2ce0ae23d546f8, corrected by cmd-ff8fa655b9244333 and cmd-2e05ae58e0894240); temporary invalid or semantically incorrect gateway reject rules, later replaced (cmd-a0e22aff2c504ac4, cmd-39e33ed9bc2c4b2b, corrected by cmd-549a8d31f8774dd5); and initial non-append backend exporters (cmd-2dadcd08ff95497a, cmd-4f2ce0ae23d546f8), which were reverted by cmd-5be8b7f40e51401d and cmd-016b540ab9894d5f and caused node2's earlier test data to be truncated during its first restart (cmd-0ac69828c7e244e8). Numerous verification payloads, responses, and TLS-test outputs remained abandoned in node1 /tmp, plus health-output files on node2 and node3; these were not cleaned. Required collector listeners and services remained healthy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2dadcd08ff95497a","cmd-4f2ce0ae23d546f8","cmd-ff8fa655b9244333","cmd-2e05ae58e0894240","cmd-a0e22aff2c504ac4","cmd-39e33ed9bc2c4b2b","cmd-549a8d31f8774dd5","cmd-0ac69828c7e244e8","cmd-5be8b7f40e51401d","cmd-016b540ab9894d5f","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied in the final observed state. The mandatory restart protocol was completed coherently on all three nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service, and post-restart functional or persistence evidence. Fixed lifecycle boot identities corroborate the final boots.","limitations":["Duplicate checks used grep -c, which counts matching lines rather than every occurrence within a line; file sizes and separate proof records support exactly-once delivery, but the test is not exhaustive for arbitrary batching or concurrency.","The initial failed download commands may have created partial /tmp artifacts before encountering 404 responses, but the trace does not directly establish their state and final lifecycle snapshots show no corresponding artifacts.","Routing behavior was demonstrated with representative payments, inventory, missing, and unsupported requests, not every possible resource layout or load pattern."]}
